Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Testing Topological Memory", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"d073459d-127b-439c-b315-94de6963b699"],

Cell["Storage capacity, retrieval accuracy, I/O performance", "Subtitle",ExpressionUUID->"74e7b6e8-0439-46d3-8fb5-ca078b2a5326"],

Cell["\<\
This test measures the memory retrieval accuracy as a function of the memory \
density.

Process: In each iteration, a new batch of random assocations A->B is stored \
in memory.
We then retrieve the same batch with inputs A and compare the outputs with B, \
measuring overlaps and Hamming distances. Optionally, random noise may be \
added to inputs A, testing the retrieval accuracy in the presence of additive \
or subtractive noise.

We use this setup to verify that different memory backends (C, Mathematica, \
Python, ...)   behave exactly the same.

Note that the native Mathematica implementation of topological associative \
memory is much slower than the performance-optimized C backend.
\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"86cc569a-be37-4aff-8a57-73ac76739a7f"],

